				"a": "The following courses are intended for students in the year after they have taken MATH 191:\n\n- Analysis 1 (MATH 201; T1)\n- Linear Algebra (MATH 230; T1)\n- Analysis 2 (MATH 202; T2; prerequisite: MATH 201)\n- Algebra 1 (MATH 231; T2; recommended prerequisite: MATH 230)\n- Multivariable Calculus (MATH 203; T3; prerequisite: MATH 202 and 230)\n- Ordinary Differential Equations (MATH 226; T3; prerequisite: MATH 202 and 230)\n\nThe following can also be taken in the year after MATH 191:\n\n- Probability (MATH 213; T2; prerequisite: prior calculus exposure, recommended: MATH 201)\n\nThere may also be mathematics elective courses that are accessible — use the course prerequisite requirements as a guide."
